target: cmd/looper/main.go
verify: go test ./cmd/looper/ -count=1 -run 'TestPrReportRefusesARunIDThatCouldForge'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    the run id is interpolated RAW into the marker and the summary line of a comment posted to a public PR, and record.Load places no constraint on `run_id`, so a store row can carry a newline and -run-id can name it. Measured against the oracle with `run_id` = "a\nb": it emits `<!-- review-loop:run=a` then `b -->`, so the HTML comment closes on the second line and swallows the first line of the body with it, and the needle push.Fingerprint matches exactly is gone. A DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE: the Python renders it. Refused at the command rather than cell()ed in Render, because cell() would rewrite the marker the push gate matches — hardening one gate by breaking the other — and Render must stay byte-comparable with the oracle over the fixture table and every run in the author's live store. The condition is DISABLED rather than deleted so `report` stays imported; a mutation that does not compile scores broken and tests nothing.
--- old
	if !report.ValidRunID(*runID) {
--- new
	if !report.ValidRunID(*runID) && false {
